WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.020
1/6: Tell Claude Code something once. In Claude Code: "Remember for the Hollybrook garden app: we store everything in SQLite, and we never use an ORM." Reply: I saved it to MindToo as a pinned instruction for the Hollybrook garden app: store all data in SQLite and never use an ORM, writing plain SQL instead.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:13.710
2/6: Ask Codex. It already knows. In Codex CLI: "Quick check before I start: which database does the Hollybrook garden app use, and should I add an ORM?" Reply: The Hollybrook garden app uses SQLite for all of its data.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:22.460
3/6: Plans change. Say so once. In Claude Code: "Update for Hollybrook: we moved from SQLite to PostgreSQL this week. Still no ORM." Reply: I updated the pinned Hollybrook instruction in MindToo.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:28.870
4/6: Codex has the update too. In Codex CLI: "Which database does Hollybrook use now?" Reply: Hollybrook now uses PostgreSQL for all application data.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.070
5/6: It all lives in MindToo, on your own computer.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.070
6/6: The earlier version is kept, not overwritten.

